IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-logic`

-- ccc12-part9-break-enter.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, "Breaking and Entering": sections 348 to 353.1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc12-part9-theft.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)").
-- Answers taken from another provision are INPUTS named for that provision (`s 2 <term>: ...`, `s 321 ...`, `s 350 ...`, `s 787(1) ...`); never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

§ `Breaking and Entering (ss 348 to 353.1)`

§§ `Section 348 -- breaking and entering`

DECLARE `s 348(3) kind of place` IS ONE OF
    `s 348(3)(a) a dwelling-house`
    `s 348(3)(b) a building or structure or any part of one, other than a dwelling-house`
    `s 348(3)(c) a railway vehicle`
    `s 348(3)(c) a vessel`
    `s 348(3)(c) an aircraft`
    `s 348(3)(c) a trailer`
    `s 348(3)(d) a pen or an enclosure in which fur-bearing animals are kept in captivity for breeding or commercial purposes`
    `s 348(3) none of those`

-- (1) "place" is defined by (3); "breaks and enters" is made of `s 321 break`, `s 350(a)` (enters) and `s 350(b)` (deemed to have broken and entered).
-- src:6850 | Breaking and entering with intent, committing offence or breaking out
-- src:6851 | 348 (1) Every one who
-- src:6852 | (a) breaks and enters a place with intent to commit an indictable offence therein,
-- src:6853 | (b) breaks and enters a place and commits an indictable offence therein, or
-- src:6854 | (c) breaks out of a place after
-- src:6855 | (i) committing an indictable offence therein, or
-- src:6856 | (ii) entering the place with intent to commit an indictable offence therein,
-- src:6857 | is guilty
-- src:6858 | (d) if the offence is committed in relation to a dwelling-house, of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life, and
-- src:6859 | (e) if the offence is committed in relation to a place other than a dwelling-house, of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years or of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 348(1) (src:6850-6859)
GIVEN `the person breaks, by s 321 the person breaks` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person enters, by s 350(a) the person enters` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed to have broken and entered, by s 350(b) the person is deemed to have broken and entered` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a place, by s 348(3) the thing is a place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has the intent to commit an indictable offence in the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person commits an indictable offence in the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person breaks out of the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person broke out after committing an indictable offence in the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person broke out after entering the place with intent to commit an indictable offence in the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 348(1) the person commits the offence of breaking and entering, or of breaking out` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `the thing is a place, by s 348(3) the thing is a place` (`ccc12 or` `paragraphs (a) and (b)` `paragraph (c)`)
    -- JUST FALSE where the thing is a definite no or no paragraph holds: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who (a) breaks and enters a place with intent to commit an indictable offence therein, (b) breaks and enters a place and commits an indictable offence therein, or (c) breaks out of a place after"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 321, s 350 or s 348(3) answer was not given and nothing else settles it
    WHERE
        `the person breaks and enters` MEANS
            `ccc12 or` (`ccc12 and` `the person breaks, by s 321 the person breaks` `the person enters, by s 350(a) the person enters`)
                       `the person is deemed to have broken and entered, by s 350(b) the person is deemed to have broken and entered`
        `paragraphs (a) and (b)` MEANS `ccc12 and` `the person breaks and enters` (JUST (`the person has the intent to commit an indictable offence in the place` OR `the person commits an indictable offence in the place`))
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS
            JUST (    `the person breaks out of the place`
                  AND (   `the person broke out after committing an indictable offence in the place`
                       OR `the person broke out after entering the place with intent to commit an indictable offence in the place`))

-- (d) a dwelling-house: an indictable offence and life; (e) any other place: indictable, not exceeding ten years, or summary.
@ref Criminal Code s 348(1) (src:6857-6859)
GIVEN `the place is a dwelling-house, by s 2 dwelling-house` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 348(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place is a dwelling-house, by s 2 dwelling-house`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for life`))   -- (d) in relation to a dwelling-house, an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for life
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST (LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (e) in relation to a place other than a dwelling-house, an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years ...
                                  , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`)   -- ... or of an offence punishable on summary conviction
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the s 2 "dwelling-house" answer was not given

-- src:6860 | Presumptions
-- src:6861 | (2) For the purposes of proceedings under this section, evidence that an accused
-- src:6862 | (a) broke and entered a place or attempted to break and enter a place is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that he broke and entered the place or attempted to do so, as the case may be, with intent to commit an indictable offence therein; or
-- src:6863 | (b) broke out of a place is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that he broke out after
-- src:6864 | (i) committing an indictable offence therein, or
-- src:6865 | (ii) entering with intent to commit an indictable offence therein.
@ref Criminal Code s 348(2) (src:6860-6865)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 348` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the accused broke and entered a place or attempted to break and enter a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 348(2)(a) the evidence is proof that the accused broke and entered the place or attempted to do so with intent to commit an indictable offence therein` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 348` AND `there is evidence that the accused broke and entered a place or attempted to break and enter a place`
    THEN IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that he broke and entered the place or attempted to do so, as the case may be, with intent to commit an indictable offence therein"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of evidence that the accused broke and entered or attempted to, in proceedings under section 348

@ref Criminal Code s 348(2) (src:6863-6865)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 348` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the accused broke out of a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 348(2)(b) the evidence is proof that the accused broke out after committing an indictable offence therein or after entering with intent to commit one` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 348` AND `there is evidence that the accused broke out of a place`
    THEN IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that he broke out after"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of evidence that the accused broke out of a place, in proceedings under section 348

-- src:6866 | Definition of place
-- src:6867 | (3) For the purposes of this section and section 351, place means
-- src:6868 | (a) a dwelling-house;
-- src:6869 | (b) a building or structure or any part thereof, other than a dwelling-house;
-- src:6870 | (c) a railway vehicle, a vessel, an aircraft or a trailer; or
-- src:6871 | (d) a pen or an enclosure in which fur-bearing animals are kept in captivity for breeding or commercial purposes.
@ref Criminal Code s 348(3) (src:6866-6871)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 348(3) kind of place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 348(3) the thing is a place` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 348(3)(a) a dwelling-house` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 348(3)(b) a building or structure or any part of one, other than a dwelling-house` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 348(3)(c) a railway vehicle` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 348(3)(c) a vessel` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 348(3)(c) an aircraft` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 348(3)(c) a trailer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 348(3)(d) a pen or an enclosure in which fur-bearing animals are kept in captivity for breeding or commercial purposes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 348(3) none of those` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "place means"

§§ `Sections 348.1 to 350 -- home invasion, unlawfully in a dwelling-house, entrance`

-- 348.1: "If a person is convicted of an offence under section 98 or 98.1, subsection 279(2) or section 343, 346 or 348 in relation to a dwelling-house, the court ... shall consider as an aggravating circumstance ..."
-- An offence outside the list is NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only"); the facts of occupation, knowledge and violence are plain inputs.
-- src:6872 | Aggravating circumstance — home invasion
-- src:6873 | 348.1 If a person is convicted of an offence under section 98 or 98.1, subsection 279(2) or section 343, 346 or 348 in relation to a dwelling-house, the court imposing the sentence on the person shall consider as an aggravating circumstance the fact that the dwelling-house was occupied at the time of the commission of the offence and that the person, in committing the offence,
-- src:6874 | (a) knew that or was reckless as to whether the dwelling-house was occupied; and
-- src:6875 | (b) used violence or threats of violence to a person or property.
@ref Criminal Code s 348.1 (src:6872-6875)
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is convicted of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is in relation to a dwelling-house, by s 2 dwelling-house` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the dwelling-house was occupied at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew that the dwelling-house was occupied or was reckless as to whether it was occupied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, in committing the offence, used violence or threats of violence to a person or property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 348.1 the court shall consider as an aggravating circumstance that the dwelling-house was occupied` MEANS
    IF    `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 98
       OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 98.1
       OR (`the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 279 AND `the offence`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
       OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 343
       OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 346
       OR `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 348
    THEN IF    `the person is convicted of the offence`
            AND `the dwelling-house was occupied at the time of the commission of the offence`
            AND `the person knew that the dwelling-house was occupied or was reckless as to whether it was occupied`
            AND `the person, in committing the offence, used violence or threats of violence to a person or property`
         THEN `the offence is in relation to a dwelling-house, by s 2 dwelling-house`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where it is definitely not in relation to a dwelling-house; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the s 2 "dwelling-house" answer was not given
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the fact that the dwelling-house was occupied at the time of the commission of the offence and that the person, in committing the offence, (a) knew that or was reckless as to whether the dwelling-house was occupied; and (b) used violence or threats of violence to a person or property" (the fact is absent: fork F-DUTY)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 98 or 98.1, subsection 279(2) or section 343, 346 or 348"; any other offence is outside the list, which the text does not close with "only"

-- src:6876 | Being unlawfully in dwelling-house
-- src:6877 | 349 (1) Every person who, without lawful excuse, enters or is in a dwelling-house with intent to commit an indictable offence in it is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years or of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 349(1) (src:6876-6877)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is a dwelling-house, by s 2 dwelling-house` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person enters or is in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the intent to commit an indictable offence in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 349(1) the person commits the offence of being unlawfully in a dwelling-house` MEANS
    IF `the person acted without lawful excuse` AND `the person enters or is in it` AND `the person has the intent to commit an indictable offence in it`
    THEN `the place is a dwelling-house, by s 2 dwelling-house`   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 2 "dwelling-house" answer was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, enters or is in a dwelling-house with intent to commit an indictable offence in it"

@ref Criminal Code s 349(1) (src:6877-6877)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 349(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6878 | Presumption
-- src:6879 | (2) For the purposes of proceedings under this section, evidence that an accused, without lawful excuse, entered or was in a dwelling-house is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that he entered or was in the dwelling-house with intent to commit an indictable offence therein.
@ref Criminal Code s 349(2) (src:6878-6879)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 349` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that the accused, without lawful excuse, entered or was in a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 349(2) the evidence is proof that the accused entered or was in the dwelling-house with intent to commit an indictable offence therein` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are proceedings under section 349` AND `there is evidence that the accused, without lawful excuse, entered or was in a dwelling-house`
    THEN IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, proof that he entered or was in the dwelling-house with intent to commit an indictable offence therein"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of evidence that the accused, without lawful excuse, entered or was in a dwelling-house, in proceedings under section 349

-- 350: "For the purposes of sections 348 and 349, (a) a person enters as soon as ... (b) a person shall be deemed to have broken and entered if ..." ("as soon as" and "if" gates: forks F-WHEN and F-DEEM)
-- src:6880 | Entrance
-- src:6881 | 350 For the purposes of sections 348 and 349,
-- src:6882 | (a) a person enters as soon as any part of his body or any part of an instrument that he uses is within any thing that is being entered; and
-- src:6883 | (b) a person shall be deemed to have broken and entered if
-- src:6884 | (i) he obtained entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within, or
-- src:6885 | (ii) he entered without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening.
@ref Criminal Code s 350 (src:6880-6885)
GIVEN `any part of the person's body is within the thing that is being entered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any part of an instrument that the person uses is within the thing that is being entered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 350(a) the person enters` MEANS
    IF `any part of the person's body is within the thing that is being entered` OR `any part of an instrument that the person uses is within the thing that is being entered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person enters as soon as any part of his body or any part of an instrument that he uses is within any thing that is being entered"

@ref Criminal Code s 350(b) (src:6883-6885)
GIVEN `the person obtained entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person entered without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 350(b) the person is deemed to have broken and entered` MEANS
    IF `the person obtained entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within` OR `the person entered without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person shall be deemed to have broken and entered if (i) he obtained entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within, or (ii) he entered without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening"

§§ `Sections 351 to 353.1 -- instruments, disguise, master keys, vehicle identification numbers`

-- src:6886 | Possession of break-in instrument
-- src:6887 | 351 (1) Every person who, without lawful excuse, has in their possession any instrument suitable for the purpose of breaking into any place, motor vehicle, vault or safe knowing that the instrument has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose,
-- src:6888 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:6889 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 351(1) (src:6886-6889)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has in their possession any instrument suitable for the purpose of breaking into any place, motor vehicle, vault or safe` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the instrument has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(1) the person commits the offence of possessing a break-in instrument` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful excuse`
      AND `the person has in their possession any instrument suitable for the purpose of breaking into any place, motor vehicle, vault or safe`
      AND `the person knows that the instrument has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, has in their possession any instrument suitable for the purpose of breaking into any place, motor vehicle, vault or safe knowing that the instrument has been used or is intended to be used for that purpose"

@ref Criminal Code s 351(1) (src:6888-6889)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 351(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction

-- src:6890 | Disguise with intent
-- src:6891 | (2) Every person who, with intent to commit an indictable offence, has their face masked or coloured or is otherwise disguised is guilty of
-- src:6892 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:6893 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 351(2) (src:6890-6893)
GIVEN `the person acted with intent to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has their face masked or coloured or is otherwise disguised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(2) the person commits the offence of being disguised with intent to commit an indictable offence` MEANS
    IF `the person acted with intent to commit an indictable offence` AND `the person has their face masked or coloured or is otherwise disguised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, with intent to commit an indictable offence, has their face masked or coloured or is otherwise disguised"

@ref Criminal Code s 351(2) (src:6892-6893)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 351(2) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6894 | Possession of instruments for breaking into coin-operated or currency exchange devices
-- src:6895 | 352 Every person who, without lawful excuse, has in their possession any instrument suitable for the purpose of breaking into a coin-operated device or a currency exchange device, knowing that the instrument has been used or is or was intended to be used for that purpose, is guilty of
-- src:6896 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:6897 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 352 (src:6894-6897)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has in their possession any instrument suitable for the purpose of breaking into a coin-operated device or a currency exchange device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the instrument has been used or is or was intended to be used for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 352 the person commits the offence of possessing an instrument for breaking into a coin-operated or currency exchange device` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful excuse`
      AND `the person has in their possession any instrument suitable for the purpose of breaking into a coin-operated device or a currency exchange device`
      AND `the person knows that the instrument has been used or is or was intended to be used for that purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, has in their possession any instrument suitable for the purpose of breaking into a coin-operated device or a currency exchange device, knowing that the instrument has been used or is or was intended to be used for that purpose"

@ref Criminal Code s 352 (src:6896-6897)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 352 the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6898 | Selling, etc., automobile master key
-- src:6899 | 353 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:6900 | (a) sells, offers for sale or advertises in a province an automobile master key otherwise than under the authority of a licence issued by the Attorney General of that province, or
-- src:6901 | (b) purchases or has in his possession in a province an automobile master key otherwise than under the authority of a licence issued by the Attorney General of that province.
@ref Criminal Code s 353(1) (src:6898-6901)
GIVEN `the thing is an automobile master key, by s 353(5) the thing is an automobile master key` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person sells, offers for sale or advertises it in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person purchases it or has it in their possession in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acted under the authority of a licence issued by the Attorney General of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(1) the person commits the offence of dealing in an automobile master key without a licence` MEANS
    IF (`the person sells, offers for sale or advertises it in a province` OR `the person purchases it or has it in their possession in a province`) AND NOT `the person acted under the authority of a licence issued by the Attorney General of that province`
    THEN `the thing is an automobile master key, by s 353(5) the thing is an automobile master key`   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): where the answer of subsection (5) was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "otherwise than under the authority of a licence issued by the Attorney General of that province"

@ref Criminal Code s 353(1) (src:6899-6899)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 353(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`)
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:6902 | Exception
-- src:6903 | (1.1) A police officer specially authorized by the chief of the police force to possess an automobile master key is not guilty of an offence under subsection (1) by reason only that the police officer possesses an automobile master key for the purposes of the execution of the police officer’s duties.
@ref Criminal Code s 353(1.1) (src:6902-6903)
GIVEN `the person is a police officer specially authorized by the chief of the police force to possess an automobile master key` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the police officer possesses an automobile master key for the purposes of the execution of the police officer's duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(1.1) the police officer is guilty of an offence under subsection (1) by reason only of possessing an automobile master key for the purposes of the execution of the police officer's duties` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a police officer specially authorized by the chief of the police force to possess an automobile master key`
      AND `the police officer possesses an automobile master key for the purposes of the execution of the police officer's duties`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A police officer specially authorized by the chief of the police force to possess an automobile master key is not guilty of an offence under subsection (1) by reason only that the police officer possesses an automobile master key for the purposes of the execution of the police officer’s duties"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is for a specially authorized police officer who possesses the key for the purposes of the execution of the officer's duties; for anyone else it says nothing

-- src:6904 | Terms and conditions of licence
-- src:6905 | (2) A licence issued by the Attorney General of a province as described in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) may contain such terms and conditions relating to the sale, offering for sale, advertising, purchasing, having in possession or use of an automobile master key as the Attorney General of that province may prescribe.
@ref Criminal Code s 353(2) (src:6904-6905)
GIVEN `the licence was issued by the Attorney General of a province as described in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term or condition relates to the sale, offering for sale, advertising, purchasing, having in possession or use of an automobile master key` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General of that province has prescribed the term or condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(2) the licence may contain the term or condition` MEANS
    IF    `the licence was issued by the Attorney General of a province as described in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)`
      AND `the term or condition relates to the sale, offering for sale, advertising, purchasing, having in possession or use of an automobile master key`
      AND `the Attorney General of that province has prescribed the term or condition`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a licence "may contain such terms and conditions ... as the Attorney General of that province may prescribe"; outside that limit the subsection grants nothing and denies nothing

-- src:6906 | Fees
-- src:6907 | (2.1) The Attorney General of a province may prescribe fees for the issue or renewal of licences as described in paragraph (1)(a) or (b).
@ref Criminal Code s 353(2.1) (src:6906-6907)
GIVEN `the fee is for the issue or renewal of a licence as described in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(2.1) the Attorney General of a province may prescribe the fee` MEANS
    IF `the fee is for the issue or renewal of a licence as described in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is "for the issue or renewal of licences as described in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)"

-- src:6908 | Record to be kept
-- src:6909 | (3) Every one who sells an automobile master key
-- src:6910 | (a) shall keep a record of the transaction showing the name and address of the purchaser and particulars of the licence issued to the purchaser as described in paragraph (1)(b); and
-- src:6911 | (b) shall produce the record for inspection at the request of a peace officer.
@ref Criminal Code s 353(3) (src:6908-6911)
GIVEN `the person sells an automobile master key` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(3) the person shall keep a record of the transaction and produce it for inspection` MEANS
    IF `the person sells an automobile master key`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who sells an automobile master key" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)

@ref Criminal Code s 353(3) (src:6910-6910)
GIVEN `the record shows the name and address of the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record shows particulars of the licence issued to the purchaser as described in paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(3)(a) the record kept is a record of the transaction showing what the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the record shows the name and address of the purchaser` AND `the record shows particulars of the licence issued to the purchaser as described in paragraph (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall keep a record of the transaction showing the name and address of the purchaser and particulars of the licence issued to the purchaser as described in paragraph (1)(b)"

@ref Criminal Code s 353(3) (src:6911-6911)
GIVEN `the person sells an automobile master key` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a peace officer requests the record for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(3)(b) the person shall produce the record for inspection` MEANS
    IF `the person sells an automobile master key` AND `a peace officer requests the record for inspection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall produce the record for inspection at the request of a peace officer" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)

-- src:6912 | Failure to comply with subsection (3)
-- src:6913 | (4) Every one who fails to comply with subsection (3) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 353(4) (src:6912-6913)
GIVEN `the person sells an automobile master key` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(4) the person commits the offence of failing to comply with subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the person sells an automobile master key` AND `the person fails to comply with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every one who fails to comply with subsection (3) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction"

@ref Criminal Code s 353(4) (src:6913-6913)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 353(4) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- "is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction": one limb, the summary one

-- src:6916 | automobile master key includes a key, pick, rocker key or other instrument designed or adapted to operate the ignition or other switches or locks of a series of motor vehicles. (passe-partout d’automobile)
@ref Criminal Code s 353(5) automobile master key (src:6916)
GIVEN `it is a key, pick, rocker key or other instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designed or adapted to operate the ignition or other switches or locks of a series of motor vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(5) the thing is an automobile master key` MEANS
    IF `it is a key, pick, rocker key or other instrument` AND `it is designed or adapted to operate the ignition or other switches or locks of a series of motor vehicles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "automobile master key includes a key, pick, rocker key or other instrument designed or adapted to operate the ignition or other switches or locks of a series of motor vehicles" does not close the list

-- src:6917 | licence includes any authorization. (licence)
@ref Criminal Code s 353(5) licence (src:6917)
GIVEN `it is an authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(5) the thing is a licence` MEANS
    IF `it is an authorization`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "licence includes any authorization" does not close the list

-- src:6920 | Definition of vehicle identification number
-- src:6921 | (2) For the purpose of this section, vehicle identification number means any number or other mark placed on a motor vehicle for the purpose of distinguishing it from other similar motor vehicles.
@ref Criminal Code s 353.1(2) (src:6920-6921)
GIVEN `it is a number or other mark placed on a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is placed for the purpose of distinguishing it from other similar motor vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353.1(2) the number or mark is a vehicle identification number` MEANS
    IF `it is a number or other mark placed on a motor vehicle` AND `it is placed for the purpose of distinguishing it from other similar motor vehicles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "vehicle identification number means any number or other mark placed on a motor vehicle for the purpose of distinguishing it from other similar motor vehicles"

-- src:6918 | Tampering with vehicle identification number
-- src:6919 | 353.1 (1) Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, wholly or partially alters, removes or obliterates a vehicle identification number on a motor vehicle.
@ref Criminal Code s 353.1(1) (src:6918-6919)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person wholly or partially alters, removes or obliterates the number or mark` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number or mark is a vehicle identification number, by s 353.1(2) the number or mark is a vehicle identification number` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353.1(1) the person commits the offence of tampering with a vehicle identification number` MEANS
    IF `the person acted without lawful excuse` AND `the person wholly or partially alters, removes or obliterates the number or mark`
    THEN `ccc12 and` `the number or mark is a vehicle identification number, by s 353.1(2) the number or mark is a vehicle identification number` `the vehicle is a motor vehicle, by s 2 motor vehicle`
         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the s 353.1(2) or s 2 "motor vehicle" answer was not given
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, wholly or partially alters, removes or obliterates a vehicle identification number on a motor vehicle"

-- src:6922 | Exception
-- src:6923 | (3) Despite subsection (1), it is not an offence to wholly or partially alter, remove or obliterate a vehicle identification number on a motor vehicle during regular maintenance or any repair or other work done on the vehicle for a legitimate purpose, including a modification of the vehicle.
@ref Criminal Code s 353.1(3) (src:6922-6923)
GIVEN `the person wholly or partially alters, removes or obliterates a vehicle identification number on a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person did so during regular maintenance or any repair or other work done on the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work was done for a legitimate purpose, including a modification of the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353.1(3) the person commits an offence under subsection (1) by altering, removing or obliterating the number during regular maintenance or repair done for a legitimate purpose` MEANS
    IF    `the person wholly or partially alters, removes or obliterates a vehicle identification number on a motor vehicle`
      AND `the person did so during regular maintenance or any repair or other work done on the vehicle`
      AND `the work was done for a legitimate purpose, including a modification of the vehicle`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Despite subsection (1), it is not an offence to wholly or partially alter, remove or obliterate a vehicle identification number on a motor vehicle during regular maintenance or any repair or other work done on the vehicle for a legitimate purpose, including a modification of the vehicle"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception is for regular maintenance, repair or other work done for a legitimate purpose; outside it the subsection says nothing

-- src:6924 | Punishment
-- src:6925 | (4) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:6926 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:6927 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 353.1(4) (src:6924-6927)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 353.1(4) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)   -- (a) indictable offence, imprisonment for a term of not more than five years
       , `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction
